 "asked_at": "2026-10-17T08:45+08:00",
 "answer": "**Yes—if you’re generally healthy, a jog in Penang looks reasonable right now.** As of **8:00 a.m. Malaysia time on October 17**, Penang’s reported readings were **53–73 on Malaysia’s Air Pollutant Index**, all in the *moderate* range. A separate George Town reading was **84 on the U.S. AQI scale**, also *moderate*. Those are different scales, so don’t compare the numbers directly. ([semakapi.my](https://semakapi.my/en/pulau-pinang))\n\nIf you have asthma or a heart or lung condition, make it a short, easy run or exercise indoors instead. Stop if the air irritates your breathing, and **recheck the reading just before you head out**—conditions can change. Malaysia’s environment department lists no general outdoor-activity restriction at moderate API levels. ([doe.gov.my](https://www.doe.gov.my/wp-content/uploads/2021/10/General-Information-of-Air-Pollutant-Index.pdf?utm_source=openai))",
